2025-05-01 03:22:22 - Thread-1361 (execute) - INFO - [Exploration]
Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• Movie.MID: primary movie identifier, used to join to the various M_* junction tables.  
• Movie.year: contains the release‐year information (take the last 4 characters → integer).  
• M_Cast.MID: connects each movie to its cast members.  
• M_Cast.PID: connects a cast row to a concrete person.  
• Person.PID: primary person identifier for joining with M_Cast.  
• Person.Gender: needed to decide whether a person counts as “Female” (allowed) or not (Male / NULL / 'None' / anything else).  

Conditions / filters you will need later  
• CAST(SUBSTR(Movie.year,‑4) AS INTEGER)  — extract the numeric year.  
• Person.Gender = 'Female'                 — keep only female actors.  
• Person.Gender IS NULL OR Person.Gender <> 'Female' — flag non‑female presence.  
• GROUP BY MID to decide if a whole movie’s cast is exclusively female (i.e., COUNT(non‑female)==0 and COUNT(all)>0).  

Exploratory SQL – step by step (LIMIT 20 on each)  

```sql
-- 1. Distinct raw values stored in Movie.year (inspect formatting)
SELECT DISTINCT "year"
FROM "Movie"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Extract the last 4 characters of Movie.year and display a sample of years
SELECT "MID",
       CAST(SUBSTR("year", -4) AS INTEGER) AS release_year
FROM "Movie"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Look at the gender value spectrum in Person
SELECT DISTINCT "Gender"
FROM "Person"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Join Movie → M_Cast → Person to see one row per performer and his/her gender
SELECT mc."MID",
       p."PID",
       p."Gender"
FROM   "M_Cast" AS mc
JOIN   "Person" AS p ON mc."PID" = p."PID"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Count how many cast members each movie has
SELECT mc."MID",
       COUNT(*) AS total_cast
FROM   "M_Cast" AS mc
GROUP  BY mc."MID"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. For every movie, count how many non‑female performers exist
SELECT mc."MID",
       SUM(CASE WHEN (p."Gender" IS NULL OR p."Gender" <> 'Female')
                THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS non_female_cnt
FROM   "M_Cast"  AS mc
JOIN   "Person"  AS p ON mc."PID" = p."PID"
GROUP  BY mc."MID"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Identify movies whose entire cast is female (non_female_cnt == 0)
SELECT t."MID"
FROM (
        SELECT mc."MID",
               SUM(CASE WHEN (p."Gender" IS NULL OR p."Gender" <> 'Female')
                        THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS non_female_cnt,
               COUNT(*) AS cast_cnt
        FROM   "M_Cast" AS mc
        JOIN   "Person" AS p ON mc."PID" = p."PID"
        GROUP  BY mc."MID"
     ) AS t
WHERE  t.non_female_cnt = 0
  AND  t.cast_cnt        > 0
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Total number of movies released in each year
SELECT CAST(SUBSTR(m."year", -4) AS INTEGER) AS yr,
       COUNT(*) AS movies_in_year
FROM   "Movie" AS m
GROUP  BY yr
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Number of exclusively‑female‑cast movies per year
WITH female_only AS (
     SELECT mc."MID"
     FROM   "M_Cast" AS mc
     JOIN   "Person" AS p ON mc."PID" = p."PID"
     GROUP  BY mc."MID"
     HAVING SUM(CASE WHEN (p."Gender" IS NULL OR p."Gender" <> 'Female')
                     THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) = 0
)
SELECT CAST(SUBSTR(m."year", -4) AS INTEGER) AS yr,
       COUNT(*) AS female_only_movies
FROM   female_only fo
JOIN   "Movie"  m ON fo."MID" = m."MID"
GROUP  BY yr
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Final query: year, total movies, percentage with exclusively female actors
WITH female_only AS (
     SELECT mc."MID"
     FROM   "M_Cast" AS mc
     JOIN   "Person" AS p ON mc."PID" = p."PID"
     GROUP  BY mc."MID"
     HAVING SUM(CASE WHEN (p."Gender" IS NULL OR p."Gender" <> 'Female')
                     THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) = 0
),
movie_year AS (
     SELECT "MID",
            CAST(SUBSTR("year", -4) AS INTEGER) AS yr
     FROM   "Movie"
)
SELECT my.yr                                           AS year,
       COUNT(*)                                        AS total_movies,
       ROUND(100.0 * SUM(CASE WHEN fo."MID" IS NOT NULL THEN 1 ELSE 0 END)
                     / COUNT(*), 2)                    AS pct_exclusive_female
FROM   movie_year my
LEFT  JOIN female_only fo ON fo."MID" = my."MID"
GROUP BY my.yr
ORDER BY my.yr
LIMIT 20;
```
